'''Hanasaka Cat''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS]] gacha event. He was added in [[Version 13.7 Update|Version 13.7]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 769
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Hanasaka Cat
|name2 = Ravenous Cherry
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ravenous Cherry''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Like the other [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|ULTRA SOULS]], Hanasaka Cat has significantly different stats between Normal (spammable) and Evolved Form (high performance), both of which can be used effectively depending on the situation.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Hanasaka Cat is a tanker or pseudo-meatshield that is Resistant to [[Angel Enemies|Angel]] and [[Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] enemies. Basically, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] into one unit. Hanasaka Cat's health is very high, up to 113,050 HP for Angel and Zombies at level 30, but he has a higher cost and recharge time than either of the aforementioned cats. Hanasaka Cat has good DPS, making him pretty good at his role as a Tanker. He can help counter stages such as [[Parade of the Dead (Deadly)|Parade of the Dead]], acting like a meatshield against the Angels and Zombies.

Hanasaka also has a 30% chance to [[freeze]] for 2 seconds. It mainly provides a small boost to his survivability, but could potentially be stacked, though this is rather pointless considering there are already better options for freezing Angels and Zombies.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Ravenous Cherry gains another knockback to help it reposition instead of taking all of the damage. It now turns Parade of the Dead into a cakewalk, with nearly as much effective health as [[King Gamereon]], almost reaching a whopping 1 million HP against Angels and Zombies at level 30. Its DPS is a lackluster 4,000, so don't use it as your only offense; support it with [[:Category:Backliner-class Cats|backliners]] or [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]].

Ravenous Cherry's crowd-control skills are at 50%, making it [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway]]-like. Its [[Conjure|Conjured]] Spirit offers additional crowd-control, knocking back all enemies and also weakening them to 50% for 6 seconds.

Upon evolving, it also becomes part of the [[Primal Fear (Combo)|Primal Fear]] [[Cat Combo]], which provides a solid boost to the effective HP of it and any other units with the [[Resistant]] ability, most notably [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]]. The other [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|two]] [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|units]] in this Combo are staples of anti-Zombie loadouts, so Ravenous Cherry can be brought alongside them to enhance the performance of Shigong and similar units while also acting as a decent backup tank.

