==Trivia==
*Hanasaka Cat is based on the story of [[wikipedia:Hanasaka Jiisan|Hanasaka Jiisan]], in which a childless couple's dead dog instructs the couple through a dream to build a mortar, which rewards the married couple with gold. The mortar is smashed and burned by a jealous neighbor, but another dream tells the husband to sprinkle the mortar's ashes on cherry trees, making them sprout beautifully and causing the couple to receive gifts from their landlord. The dead dog is represented by Ravenous Cherry's dog-like Conjured Spirit.
*Hanasaka Cat is the only [[Ancient Heroes ULTRA SOULS (Gacha Event)|Ultra Soul]] whose name contains the word "Cat". This localization is particularly unusual because Hanasaka Cat's Japanese name is simply Hanasaka Jiisan, the folktale he's based on.
*[[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Masked Yulala]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] and Hanasaka Cat all have similar movement animations.
*The word 怪樹 ''Kaiju'' ("Strange Tree") in Ravenous Cherry's Japanese name is a pun on 怪獣 ''[[wikipedia:Kaiju|kaijū]]'' ("strange beast").
*POCH-1 is a pun on ''Pochi'', a common name for pet dogs in Japan, as the nutrient that gave Ravenous Cherry its appetite came from Hanasaka Cat's dog.
*Ravenous Cherry may be a reference to [https://wikizilla.org/wiki/Biollante Biollante Flower Beast Form] from the ''[[wikipedia:Godzilla (franchise)|Godzilla]]'' franchise.
*The three sharp-toothed plants at Ravenous Cherry's base resemble [[mariowiki:Piranha Plant|Piranha Plants]] from the ''[[wikipedia:Mario (franchise)|Mario]]'' franchise.

